# Competitor vocabulary and commercial-only papers (hard rule)

Operator directive (Phil, 2026-09-24), verbatim intent:

> **Hard rule: always use competitor's vocabulary. Never make your own
> words up for well known industry terms. If you don't know the word or
> measure, you must research what competitors use. Only use commercial
> language. Remove musings everywhere about honesty and other value
> judgements in documents. The demand to remove musings was made
> multiple times and is getting ignored. Do not ignore the musings
> rule ever again.**

## The rule

> **On every go-to-market, price list, kit, canvas, contract, and other
> customer- or partner-facing commercial document: use only commercial
> vocabulary that Competitors already use for that meter, package, or
> discount. Never invent labels for well-known industry concepts. If
> the term or measure is unknown, research CyberArk, Delinea,
> BeyondTrust, and peer PAM / identity vendors (and Microsoft for
> channel language) before writing. Commercial documents contain
> commercial terms only - no honesty banners, no Met / certified /
> assessment-ready self-policing, no agent value judgements, no LLM
> sidenotes. Agents still obey honesty in chat and internal rules;
> they must not paste that policing into the paper.**

This rule does **not** weaken
[`compliance-claims-honesty.mdc`](compliance-claims-honesty.mdc) for
agents in chat, commits, or product chrome. It forbids putting those
guardrails **into** commercial documents.

Vendor names stay out of website and customer price-list **bodies**
([`no-competitor-names-in-website.mdc`](no-competitor-names-in-website.mdc)).
Research and commit bodies may name vendors. Customer papers say
**Competitors** when a generic reference is required.

## Vocabulary - research first

| Forbidden (AIC-invented or non-commercial) | Prefer (Competitors' commercial shape) |
| --- | --- |
| Estate / Campus as package or SKU names | Edition packages: Basic / Standard / Enterprise; Professional / Premium / Platinum (or AIC edition names that match that shape) |
| Estate as a sold meter | Named user, privileged user, asset, endpoint, system, target |
| Size band / volume band as coined product language | Volume discount, quantity discount, list price, prepaid term discount |
| Freemium / "no freemium SKU" asides | Omit the word and the aside. The operator-approved free offer (2026-10-09) is named "Free plan" (AIC-CMMC-FREE); partner licenses are "not-for-resale (NFR)". Do not add other free SKUs without operator approval |
| Hard-cap musings, "not in Year 1 totals" LLM asides | State included quantities and list add-ons in plain commercial lines |
| Honesty / Met / OSA certify / assessment-ready banners on price papers | Omit from the paper. Warranty allocation in counsel voice belongs in License / Product Terms only |

If a measure is not on a published competitor price sheet (Texas DIR,
GSA / Carahsoft, buyer-guide unit rates), **do not invent a new meter
name**. Use the closest Competitors meter or "quote."

Canonical research notes (internal):
`pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/competitive/enterprise-pam-competitor-packaging.md`,
`pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/pricing/pim-pam-pum-competitor-guide.md`.

## Musings - never again on commercial documents

Operative surfaces include (non-exhaustive):

- `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/pricing/**`
- `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/contracts/**` (including kits)
- `pam-platform-docs/docs/go-to-market/canvases/**` when they are
  customer- or partner-facing price / offer surfaces
- Any future End User License Agreement (EULA), price list, rate card,
  or marketplace offer text

**Delete on sight** from those surfaces:

- "This does not certify / does not stamp Met / not assessment-ready"
- "Honesty." sections and assessor-judges-OSA banners on price lists
- Prompt restatements, open-q, TODO for agents, "do not invent features"
- Value judgements ("compelling," "bizarre," self-policing hard-cap essays)
- LLM commentary about prior agent mistakes

Legal warranty and risk allocation in counsel voice (License / Product
Terms) remains allowed - that is commercial contract language, not an
agent musing. See
[`no-llm-sidenotes-in-contracts.mdc`](no-llm-sidenotes-in-contracts.mdc).

Coverage matrices may state **kit provides**, **customer**, **manual**,
or **other product** as factual commercial columns. They must not wrap
every row in Met / OSA honesty sermons.

## Required agent behavior

1. Before adding a meter, package name, or discount label: check what
   Competitors publish. If unsure, research; do not coin.
2. Before finishing any GTM / price / kit edit: grep for honesty,
   Met, assessment-ready, freemium, estate (as SKU), size-band,
   hard cap musings, "does not certify." Delete hits on commercial
   surfaces.
3. Keep agent honesty in chat and Cursor rules. Never copy it into
   the signed or sold paper.
4. Mirror this file to `core-assets/.cursor/rules/` in the same
   change set ([`auto-commit-push.mdc`](auto-commit-push.mdc)).

